            <ArticleTitle>Isolated left coronary ostial stenosis as a result of fibromuscular dysplasia in a young man.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>988-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 28-year-old man was admitted to hospital for investigation of a 2-week history of angina occurring on exertion. Coronary angiography showed an isolated left coronary ostial stenosis and left main trunk plasty was performed 2 weeks later. The pathological diagnosis of the left coronary ostial stenosis was fibromuscular dysplasia, which makes this a rare case.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
